# Copy this file to `.env` in the same folder (`mobile/`) and set your PC's address.
# Restart Expo after any change (`npx expo start`).
#
# Physical phone (same Wi‑Fi as PC): your PC's LAN IPv4, e.g.:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.42:5000
#
# Android emulator (host machine from the emulator):
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:5000
#
# iOS Simulator on Mac (often works for a server on the Mac):
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5000
#
# Android + USB (after `npm run adb:reverse` from `mobile/`):
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5000
#
# Phone and PC NOT on the same LAN (e.g. only mobile data, or different Wi‑Fi than the PC):
#   A LAN IP like 192.168.x.x will NOT work — the phone cannot reach your house PC.
#   Options: (1) Put PC and phone on the same Wi‑Fi/hotspot, (2) USB + adb reverse + URL above,
#   (3) Tailscale/ZeroTier on both devices, then use the PC’s tailnet IP, e.g.:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://100.x.y.z:5000
#   (4) Tunnel Flask with ngrok/cloudflared and put that https URL here (must allow HTTP from app if only https).
#
# Placeholder — replace MY_LAN_IP with your PC LAN IPv4 for same-Wi‑Fi phone testing, e.g.:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.42:5000
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://MY_LAN_IP:5000
#
# Location (expo-location): allow foreground location when the app asks.
# Technician nearby list: distance_km and radius filter need GPS (fetchTechnicianNearbyRequests).
# Technician request detail: distance_km is returned only when the app sends ?lat=&lng= (device GPS).
# Customer create request: map pin is required; POST sends latitude & longitude (multipart or JSON),
#   field names match Flask _create_request_payload_from_multipart / customer_create_request.
#
# Android emulator mock location (Extended controls → Location, or adb):
#   Riyadh map default (create-request map UI): adb emu geo fix 46.6753 24.7136
#   Demo seed pending job (distance E2E after seed_demo.py): adb emu geo fix 46.6753 24.7136
# iOS Simulator: Features → Location → Custom (lat/lng) — use coords above for the scenario you test.
#
# Maps (react-native-maps): optional for local dev in Expo Go / iOS Simulator (Apple Maps).
# Required for Android native builds (prebuild / APK) — enable "Maps SDK for Android" in Google Cloud,
# restrict the key to your app package + SHA-1, then set:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=your_android_maps_key
# Re-run prebuild or rebuild the dev client after changing this value.

# Portfolio upload limits are enforced by the API (`GET /api/v1/me/portfolio` returns `limits`).
# Optional env knobs live in the Flask `.env` — see repo root `.env.example`.
